<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40482" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Raurăci</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Raurĭci</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 17, 31, § 106</span></i>),
			ōrum, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Gaul</i>, <i>on the Rhine</i>, <i>neighbors of the
				Helvetians</i>, <i>near Basle</i>, <i><span class="en">Caes. B. G. 1,
				5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7,
			75</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Raurăcum</span></b> ,
			i, n., <i>the city of the
				Rauraci</i>, now <i>Augst</i>, <i>near Basle</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 10, 6</span></i>:
			Rauriaca colonia, Plin. l. l.; also called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Raurĭcum</span></b> , <i><span class="en">id.
				4, 12, 24, § 79</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">RAVRICA,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 432</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Raurăcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Rauraci</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">colonia Rauraca = Rauracum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					4, 17, 31, § 106</span></i>
			 (al. Rauriaca).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
